WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.102
-Thank you.
-Look at you.

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:06.172
Hasan, look at you on TV holding
your own with Reese Witherspoon.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.773
-We're back!
-I want to get in --

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:09.675
We're back.
-We're back on TV.

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:10.810
-Yes, we are.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.278
-Live audience.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:13.713
-Live audience.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.348
-Feel great.
-Dude, you're busy.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:17.083
-Dude, we had a busy pandemic.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.152
-You had a very busy --

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:22.087
-Productive. My wife and I,
we had our baby, second baby.

00:00:22.087 --> 00:00:24.590
Yes. Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.192
-That's the best!
-Now, listen,

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.760
I haven't told anybody
this, Jimmy.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.264
This is news for a lot
of people, but my wife and I,

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:33.366
we were actually having
fertility problems for years.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.567
And that was really tough on us,

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:38.271
and it loaded the relationship
with a lot of tension.

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:39.605
-Of course, sure.

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:41.140
-And, you know, we'd be
sitting there late at night

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.842
having really tough
conversations.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.910
You know, are we going
to be able to have kids?

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.746
Are we arrogant
for thinking we deserve kids?

00:00:47.746 --> 00:00:50.249
And I was trying to,
you know, be optimistic.

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:53.853
I go, "Babe, what if we adopt?"
Right?

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.889
-Yeah.
-What if we adopt a white baby

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.623
just to flex
on these mother [bleep]

00:00:57.623 --> 00:01:00.026
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:03.329
Just to show people we really
made it in this country!

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.897
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:04.897 --> 00:01:08.334
And we'll show him off!

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.802
Take him to parties.

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:11.437
-No.
-"Hi, I'm Bradley.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.973
I'm a proud member of
the Indian-American community."

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:16.943
"This is my son! Bradley!"

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:19.311
-Flex.
-For $15 a day,

00:01:19.311 --> 00:01:23.849
Bradley goes to the Gymboree
on the Upper West Side.

00:01:23.849 --> 00:01:25.084
-The Gymboree.

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:27.086
-We saved him

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:30.723
from a war-torn part
of America -- Detroit.

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.059
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:35.894
And she told me,
"I want a baby with you.

00:01:35.894 --> 00:01:37.229
It is not my ovaries.

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:39.465
You have got to go
get your balls checked out."

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:41.400
-Okay.
-Now, listen, listen --

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:46.539
I'm at that age now where a lot
of doctors are my age, okay?

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.608
-Okay.
-And they're Indian,

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:51.678
which means I might know them.

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.213
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:57.183
So, I'm sitting over here
at the fertility clinic.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:00.086
Nurse comes out. She's like,
"Dr. Shah will see you now.

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:03.389
I'm like, "This better not
be Arjan Shah."

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.890
Okay? Door opens.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.460
I hear a familiar voice.
He's like, "Hasan Minhaj?"

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.995
I'm like, this is Arjan Shah!

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:11.130
This kid is an idiot.
I grew up with him.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.431
-No, you're jok--
-Yes,

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:16.102
he failed out of the Caribbean
med school twice, Jimmy.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.304
-This is so you.
This could only happen to you.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:21.340
-Yeah, I go, "Arjan,
how are you licensed?"

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:22.909
He's like, "I don't know.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.777
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:27.180
That's why I'm a jizz doctor
on the Upper West Side."

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.514
-Okay, well, I don't --

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:29.816
There's probably
a different name for it.

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:31.150
-"Drop your pants.
How's Auntie?"

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.752
I'm like, "Don't bring
my mom into this."

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:33.919
This is crazy.

00:02:33.919 --> 00:02:35.121
He's not even an M.D.

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:38.191
Jimmy, he's a D.O.
I'm like, this guy

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:39.592
can't even afford
all the good letters.

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.727
Oh, you don't know this.
-No, what's a D.O.?

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:44.396
-There's a war going on
in the medical community, guys,

00:02:44.396 --> 00:02:46.365
between M.D.s and D.O.s.

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:49.702
-I don't know D.O.
-No, okay, so it's like --

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:53.172
They're basically the same,
but they're totally not.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:56.275
Like, an M.D. is Coca-Cola,

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:58.010
and a D.O. is RC Cola.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:02:59.345
You understand?

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.846
It's like an off-brand doctor.

00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:03.649
Like John Oliver is an M.D.
I'm a D.O.

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:05.351
We're the same,
but we're totally not.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.886
-No, you're an M.D.

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:09.789
-Listen, so, you know,
Arjan comes in there.

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:13.693
And, you know, he's like,
"Listen, man, if you --"

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.327
He's feeling around
my merchandise.

00:03:15.327 --> 00:03:17.764
And he goes, "Oh, you --

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:19.031
You have too much blood
down there.

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:20.900
It's been lowering
your sperm count,

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.436
so we're going to have to do
a very dangerous surgery.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:25.738
It's called varicocele
repair surgery.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:28.241
But don't worry, bro,
I'll be doing the surgery."

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:29.608
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.608 --> 00:03:30.943
I'm like, "Arjan,
I'm very worried.

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:32.311
You're in a lab coat
and Jordans."

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:35.280
This is not instilling
confidence in me, as a patient.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.316
-[ Laughing ] Jordans.

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:39.051
-He pulls out a trimmer, and he
goes, "Let me get up in there.

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:41.020
I'll shave you down. We'll do it
right here right now."

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.788
I go, "Arjan --"
-No, this is --

00:03:42.788 --> 00:03:44.089
-"Yeah. I know
we grew up together,

00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:46.592
but I'm not ready for this."
He goes, "Listen, man.

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:49.461
If you don't get this surgery,

00:03:49.461 --> 00:03:51.430
you can't have kids."

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:53.165
And I go, "You know what?
just give me the fade.

00:03:53.165 --> 00:03:55.802
Make the top match the bottom.
Shave me down."

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:56.936
-Give me the fade.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:59.939
-Yeah, he puts
the Darth Vader on me.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.341
Six hours later, I wake up.

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:02.909
I'm butt naked in a diaper.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.677
Four huge bloodstains
on the diaper.

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.812
I look down. I look up.

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:09.616
I see Arjan. I go, "Arjan,
I only have two testicles."

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:10.650
-Yeah.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.451
-How did you mess up
two extra times?

00:04:12.451 --> 00:04:14.220
He's like, "Don't worry, bro.
We figured it out."

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.488
-Yeah.

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:18.290
-"Just give it six weeks,
and you'll be good to go."

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:21.394
Six weeks later, we have hot
monogamous action, me and Beena.

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:23.095
She gets pregnant,
and there you go.

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:24.397
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:25.565
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:28.667
-So thank you to Arjan Shah
and the D.O.s.

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.469
-And the D.O.s.
Shout-out to the D.O.s.

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.605
-Shout-out to the D.O.s.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.306
-Dude, I want to talk
about "The Morning Show."

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:35.508
-Yes.
-'Cause this is --

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:38.711
I saw Episode 1,
and there you are crushing it,

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.045
you and Reese Witherspoon.

00:04:40.045 --> 00:04:42.281
I go, "Look at Hasan.
This is unbelievable."

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:45.218
Explain how did you get
this role and what was it like.

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:47.419
-Yeah, so I'm getting ready.

00:04:47.419 --> 00:04:49.421
It's my sister's wedding.

00:04:49.421 --> 00:04:51.290
I'm at home. I'm in Sacramento.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.025
I get a call from my agent.
He goes, "Listen, man,

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:54.793
you've been playing a fake
TV anchor for seven years.

00:04:54.793 --> 00:04:56.729
I think you can do this."

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.063
-"We want you to play
a fake TV anchor."

00:04:58.063 --> 00:05:00.966
-It's not really a stretch.
-Yeah.

00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:04.369
-"You need to be able to do
your lines and sing and dance."

00:05:04.369 --> 00:05:06.973
I call my sister. I go,
"Come downstairs right now.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:08.074
You need to read lines with me."

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:10.342
She goes, "It's kind of my day."

00:05:10.342 --> 00:05:13.646
And I go, "Yeah, yeah,
but what about me, Ayesha?"

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:16.015
-Why was it her day?
-It was her wedding weekend.

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.950
-Oh. Yeah, of course,
it is her day.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:18.984
-Yeah.
-She's right.

00:05:18.984 --> 00:05:20.919
-But I'm like, "What about...
-No.

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:24.056
...a recurring role on Season 2
of 'The Morning Show'?"

00:05:24.056 --> 00:05:25.891
-Priorities!
-Now, my mom has always wanted

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:28.727
to join SAG-AFTRA,
so she comes downstairs.

00:05:28.727 --> 00:05:32.632
And we had to sing a little duet
of "Baby It's Cold Outside."

00:05:32.632 --> 00:05:34.767
Now, my mom emigrated here
to the States in 1985.

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:37.403
She has no idea
what this song is.

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:38.937
And so we just put it on wax,

00:05:38.937 --> 00:05:40.606
and we sent it in
as my audition tape.

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:42.108
-That was your audition,
and you actually brought it

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:44.110
